<h1>John Kitover</h1>
<p>Businessman and Army National Guard veteran. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>A self-described Republican-Libertarian businessman, podcast host, and National Guard veteran who ran for Congress in the 16th District in 2026. Filed on the last day.</p>
<p><a href="https://johnkitover45.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (johnkitover45.com)</a></p>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<p>No spending report found for this campaign yet.</p>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>Not listed in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC).</p>
<h2>What they would do</h2>
<ul>
<li>Freeze the property tax levy in his first year and demand pension reform from Springfield before any new tax. <q>I will freeze the property tax levy in my first year as mayor and demand structural pension reform from Springfield before any new tax increases are considered.</q> (<a href="https://johnkitover45.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site</a>)</li>
<li>Says the city cannot borrow and spend its way out, and has floated bankruptcy over the pension debt. <q>We cannot borrow and spend our way out of this crisis.</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayor-election-candidates-2027-petitions-filed/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Oct. 2026</a>)</li>
<li>Lower taxes to attract business and slash borrowing. <q>not more debt, not more taxes, not more of the same.</q> (<a href="https://johnkitover45.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>Main points</h3>
<p>Money first: A property tax freeze in year one, no new taxes until Springfield reforms pensions, less borrowing, and bankruptcy on the table for the pension debt.</p>
<p>Business: Lower taxes as the way to bring employers back.</p>
<p>Not published: Positions on police, housing, schools, or transit beyond the budget.</p>
<h3>Next to the others</h3>
<p>Only Kitover: Bankruptcy as an answer to the pension debt.</p>
<p>Property tax freeze: Kitover, Holberg, and Giannoulias would freeze the levy; Wilson and Kelly would lower it.</p>
<p>Party: Kitover and Carter-Walters are the field&#39;s conservatives in a nonpartisan race.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Would freeze the property tax levy in his first year, refuse new taxes until the state reforms pensions, cut borrowing, and consider bankruptcy for the pension debt.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>We cannot borrow and spend our way out of this crisis.</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayor-election-candidates-2027-petitions-filed/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Oct. 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
